# Force LF line endings for the source file types `yarn lint` actually checks
# (see the `lint` script in package.json), regardless of platform or the local
# core.autocrlf setting. CI (.github/workflows/test.yml) already checks out with
# core.autocrlf=false (LF); without this, a Windows checkout with the common
# core.autocrlf=true default gets CRLF working-tree files for these extensions,
# which then fails ESLint's linebreak-style rule locally even though CI is green.
#
# Deliberately scoped to just these extensions: src/renderer/src/test/fixtures/
# holds real-world sample files (e.g. from DaVinci Resolve, Final Cut Pro,
# PotPlayer) in other formats (.edl, .csv, .vtt, .xml, .otio, ...) whose exact
# bytes - including line endings - the parsers under test may depend on, so
# they're intentionally left with no attribute and are unaffected by this file.
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
